  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I believe that showing arbitrary labels  and nametag colors creates unneeded divide between users.\n\nThe safety system is a good idea, but security by obscurity doesn't work, trolls will work it out.\n\nI suggest removing ranks (by name) leave all the nametags unified. \n\nInstead on the safety panel:\n * only disable by default dangerous stuff (shaders, particles) for people who have been reported being a nuisance\n* leave everything on by default\n* have levels, described as such:\n** player who hasn't played more than few days\n** player who has been friended and not reported by at least N people\n** player who has uploaded avatars and didn't get reported with playing it\n** people who has created world and shown it to anyone and didn't get reported\n** people with publicly available worlds\n** people with public avatars, who are used more than by N people\n** friends\nand similar.  Additionally per users avatar settings.\n\nVRChat devs, you should be more open and honest about the system, communicate with the community. And stop creating division where it shoudn't exist.",
